§ `Kinnim: the nouns`

§§ `Offerings, animals, places on the altar`

-- חטאת (hattat) and עולה (olah).
DECLARE `Offering` IS ONE OF
    `sin offering`
    `burnt offering`

-- עוף and בהמה.
DECLARE `Animal` IS ONE OF
    bird
    beast

-- Above or below the red line round the middle of the altar (חוט הסיקרא).  "למעלה / למעלן" and
-- "למטה / למטן" in the text.
DECLARE `Level` IS ONE OF
    above
    below

-- תורין and בני יונה.  The Torah allows either for a bird offering, and 2:5 forbids pairing across them.
DECLARE `Species` IS ONE OF
    turtledove
    `young pigeon`

§§ `Why a pair is brought`

-- חובה, נדר, נדבה.  An obligation is owed by law (after childbirth, a discharge and the other cases
-- the Torah names); a vow and a gift are offered of one's own will.
DECLARE `Ground of the offering` IS ONE OF
    obligation
    vow
    gift

-- The words that dedicate a voluntary burnt offering (1:1): "הרי עלי עולה" ("I take a burnt offering
-- upon myself") or "הרי זו עולה" ("this one is a burnt offering").
DECLARE `Words of dedication` IS ONE OF
    `it is upon me`
    `this one is`

-- The reason (שם, literally "name") an obligation is owed; 1:4 gives childbirth and discharge as its examples.
DECLARE `Reason for the obligation` IS ONE OF
    childbirth
    discharge
    `another reason`

§§ `A mixture of birds`

-- An obligation whose birds have not been assigned to their offerings (קן סתומה, an "unassigned
-- nest"): the owner owes so many sin offerings and so many burnt offerings, and any of its birds may
-- become either until the priest assigns it.  A whole nest of p pairs owes p of each; 3:5 also speaks of
-- an obligation one of whose birds has already been offered, which owes unequal numbers.
DECLARE `Unassigned obligation` HAS
    `sin offerings owed` IS A NUMBER
    `burnt offerings owed` IS A NUMBER

-- Birds that have become indistinguishable from one another (נתערבו).  A designated bird (מפורשת)
-- has been assigned to its offering by the owner when it was bought, or by the priest: it can only be
-- that offering.  Each unassigned obligation is one owner's (or one reason's) nest.
DECLARE `Mixture` HAS
    `designated sin offerings` IS A NUMBER
    `designated burnt offerings` IS A NUMBER
    `unassigned obligations` IS A LIST OF `Unassigned obligation`

-- Did the priest ask how the mixture should be offered (כהן נמלך, chapters 1 and 2) before offering
-- it, or did he offer it on his own (כהן שאינו נמלך, chapter 3)?
DECLARE `Whether the priest asked` IS ONE OF
    `the priest asked first`
    `the priest did not ask`

-- What a priest who did not ask did with the whole mixture (chapter 3).
DECLARE `What the priest did` IS ONE OF
    `offered all above`
    `offered all below`
    `offered half above and half below`
    `offered some other number above`

§§ `Birds that fly`

-- Where one bird of an unassigned pair went (2:1).
DECLARE `Where the bird went` IS ONE OF
    `into the air`
    `among birds that must die`
    `it died`
    `among birds that are to be offered`

-- What happened between an unassigned pair and a designated pair whose two birds had become mixed with
-- each other (2:4).
DECLARE `Flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` IS ONE OF
    `one flew from the unassigned pair to the designated pair`
    `then one flew back`
    `the first flight was from the designated pair`

-- What happened with sin offerings on one side, burnt offerings on the other and an unassigned pair
-- between them (2:5).
DECLARE `Flight from the middle` IS ONE OF
    `one flew from the middle to each side`
    `those two flew back to the middle`
    `then one flew from the middle to a side`

§§ `The vow of 3:6`

-- What is known of the two nests a woman gave the priest after vowing "a nest upon me when I bear a
-- male" and bearing a male (3:6).
DECLARE `What is known of her vow` IS ONE OF
    `she did not say which birds were for her vow`
    `she said which birds were for her vow`
    `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it`
    `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did`
